  "The Checkout Attachment Module for eCommerceGo introduces a streamlined way for customers to add attachments during the checkout process. This module empowers customers to include essential documents or files related to their orders, such as design specifications, proof of identity, or personalized instructions. By allowing attachments at checkout, the module enhances the clarity and accuracy of orders, ensuring that all necessary information is captured upfront.": "O Módulo de anexo de checkout para eCommerceGo apresenta uma maneira simplificada para os clientes adicionarem anexos durante o processo de checkout. ",
  "View Live Demo": "Ver demonstração ao vivo",
  "Intuitive Attachment Process for Customers": "Processo de anexação intuitivo para clientes",
  "Designed with user experience in mind, the Checkout Attachment Module makes adding attachments a straightforward and hassle-free process. During checkout, customers are presented with an easy-to-use interface to upload their files. Supported file types and size limits can be configured to suit your business needs, ensuring compatibility and efficiency. This user-friendly approach helps reduce friction in the checkout process, leading to higher customer satisfaction and fewer order discrepancies.": "Projetado pensando na experiência do usuário, o Módulo de Anexos do Checkout torna a adição de anexos um processo simples e descomplicado. ",
  "Enhanced Communication with Administrators": "Comunicação aprimorada com administradores",
  "Once a customer adds an attachment, it becomes immediately visible to the admin on the backend. This feature is particularly useful for businesses that require additional documentation to process orders accurately. Admins can easily access, review, and manage these attachments through the eCommerceGo admin panel. This seamless integration ensures that all relevant information is at the admin fingertips, facilitating smoother order processing and better customer service.": "Depois que um cliente adiciona um anexo, ele fica imediatamente visível para o administrador no back-end. ",
